<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Hybrid warfare: The threat of Russia looms over the Mediterranean</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a2b92e8198ef84259af4b488ba94ada043591627f212da1ba313e79cb044e9d</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:39:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-hybrid-warfare-the-threat-of-russia-looms-over-the-mediterranean" /><summary type="html">The CIA has reportedly warned several countries that Russia is preparing to launch hybrid operations across the Mediterranean Sea. But is the risk real, or is it a form of cyber warfare?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK police bail five men held over suspected bomb plot at US-run air base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81ed1e876907e498337d76e71cd15777a32b585dce2353787a3771bc3008ffc0</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:01:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-five-men-arrested-suspected-bomb-plot-uk-air-base-to-be-released-on-bail-fairford" /><summary type="html">British police said Monday that five men arrested on explosives and terror charges near a US-run air base in England were being released on bail but remained under investigation. Counter-terror detectives said they were investigating "multiple lines of inquiry", including whether there is a link to Iran.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian attacks kill eight in Ukraine after Moscow vows to continue war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224646d28e29e4c99235ea1dede3d6083a99a32097cab17a5513e599e59df0a5</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T21:55:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-strikes-kill-eight-ukraine-war-moscow" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes killed eight people across Ukraine on Sunday, authorities said, a day after Moscow vowed to continue the war. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Russia had launched about 3,900 drones, aerial bombs and missiles over the past week. Kyiv accused Moscow of deliberately targeting civilians as winter approaches.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic resigns to run for prime minister in October elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0342a19d976e9319bead911febcec820dc278a5ea9f46b07e14c805d1d67b0f1</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T18:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-serbian-president-aleksandar-vucic-resigns-expected-to-run-for-prime-minister" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic stepped down as the country's head of state Sunday, paving the way for him to run as his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party's candidate for prime minister in the October parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Non! Why the Swiss rejected stricter neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:611a725f8fe28ea7e63ed08d084b03272bd738521adf493cf22b831c4d43cd75</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:33:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260927-non-why-the-swiss-rejected-stricter-neutrality" /><summary type="html">A referendum has been held in Switzerland on whether Swiss neutrality should be more strictly enforced in the Constitution. Richard Werly, Europe correspondent for the Swiss publication Blick, tell us why the Swiss have voted "no".</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>First Protestant march in Catholic area in nearly 30 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58659693c69906e08f9fe6f7ac06f11b07424bf1f5fad8faf32a0c833a87a4da</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/first-protestant-march-in-catholic-area-in-nearly-30-years" /><summary type="html">Tensions are running high in Northern Ireland after the High Court in Belfast approved a controversial parade. Around 2,000 protesters have blocked the route into a Catholic area where the Protestant march was due to pass. It is the first time in nearly 30 years that the Orange Order has been allowed to march along this route, which was a notorious flashpoint before the 1998 Good Friday Agreement largely brought an end to the bloodshed of the Troubles. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham has appealed for calm on all sides, saying he does not want to see Northern Ireland “go backwards.”</summary></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest 5 men, counter-terror squad probes ‘major incident’ near air base used by US forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bdcd9a4f65a8020ad1da2b446254f2a6b4a99f5419e4e83e9c9946bdd430b0d</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T09:05:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-uk-police-evacuate-homes-near-air-base-used-by-us-arrest-men-on-suspected-explosives-offenses" /><summary type="html">British police said they had evacuated homes Sunday near the air base of Fairford in southwest England used by US air forces and arrested five men over suspected explosives offences. British counter-terrorism police are investigating the incident.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland court allows Orange Order march through Catholic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5de192fd86a2520a124ade3dcef902fd02e2597cf6d1bd349d6184061d22f6e9</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:41:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-court-allows-orange-order-march-through-catholic-area" /><summary type="html">A court in Northern Ireland has allowed a Protestant parade to proceed through a controversial route in a Catholic area for the first time in nearly 30 years. The legal dispute ended in the early hours of Sunday, with counterprotests now underway and police working to keep marchers and protesters apart. The Drumcree parade dispute dates back to the mid-1990s, when tensions over the route led to riots, roadblocks and murders, threatening Northern Ireland’s peace process. Hervé Amoric reports from Portadown.</summary></entry><entry><title>Switzerland votes on country's neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02bf781a2e725fa848b713d205b7f116026441cf12d1df429dc8d748150f5c0c</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:36:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/switzerland-votes-on-country-s-neutrality" /><summary type="html">As other neutral countries such as Austria and Ireland increase defence spending and strengthen ties with NATO, Swiss voters are taking part in a referendum on whether to enshrine a stricter definition of the country’s centuries-old neutrality in the constitution. Switzerland has not fought a military conflict since neutrality was established in 1815, but some argue that measures such as sanctions can undermine that principle. The vote also raises questions about how neutrality can be maintained amid Europe’s changing security landscape, with Russia at war with Ukraine and the US putting pressure on traditional alliances such as NATO. Josh Vardey reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland: Disputed parade set for flashpoint after nearly 30 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14a086d15387b67f70d579eb6ed349a5653b2c59bc476ef076f36bbc2eba6432</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:33:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/northern-ireland-disputed-parade-set-for-flashpoint-after-nearly-30-years" /><summary type="html">A court in Northern Ireland has allowed a Protestant parade to proceed through a controversial route in a Catholic area for the first time in nearly 30 years. The legal dispute ended in the early hours of Sunday, with counterprotests now underway and police working to keep marchers and protesters apart. The Drumcree parade dispute dates back to the mid-1990s, when tensions over the route led to riots, roadblocks and murders, threatening Northern Ireland’s peace process. Hervé Amoric reports from Portadown.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Russian sleeper cell’: Can Germany’s far-right AfD be barred from sensitive intel?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1e4f9ad451dc8b37ba2d2b7d42742fc418c429279c911f8641b2e1b6c3958dd</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:03:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-russian-sleeper-cell-can-germany-far-right-afd-be-barred-from-sensitive-intelligence" /><summary type="html">The prospect of an AfD-led government in Germany’s Saxony-Anhalt has exacerbated long-standing fears that the far-right Russia-friendly party may gain access to sensitive information of interest to the Kremlin, fuelling debate as to whether and how it can be barred from classified intelligence.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss reject plan to adopt stricter form of neutrality that would rule out NATO cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be8081b32f180c7878fecc89c2456480a06e685ca1a4c704369bf6aaeba21735</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T05:52:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260927-swiss-reject-plan-to-adopt-stricter-form-of-neutrality-that-would-rule-out-nato-cooperation" /><summary type="html">Swiss voters on Sunday voted against a proposal that would have imposed a more restrictive form of neutrality on the Alpine country, preventing it from levelling sanctions without UN backing or joining military alliances except when under direct attack. Switzerland's centuries-long tradition of "armed neutrality" has not prevented the government from throwing its support behind EU sanctions on Russia following Moscow's invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Maricarmen vs the 'vultures': A 'social tragedy' mobilising Spaniards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:655b332f307c8b7a27c483449efad00285ff6a815d3094f903ed666f9abe4cba</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:03:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260926-maricarmen-vs-the-vultures-a-social-tragedy-mobilising-spaniards--68b38ed468b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260926-maricarmen-vs-the-vultures-a-social-tragedy-mobilising-spaniards" /><summary type="html">Protests are ongoing in Madrid right now, with many demonstrators holding signs and banners that read "Maricarmen vs the vultures", "Maricarmen, you are not alone", or "Ni una Maricarmen más", not one more Maricarmen.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands march in Madrid to protest eviction of 87-year-old woman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:912a644d3a4b362f4684e5264387fb723c41d528318df26352d995439abe08b2</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T17:04:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-thousands-march-in-madrid-to-protest-eviction-of-87-year-old-woman" /><summary type="html">The eviction of 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal on Wednesday sparked a thousands-strong protest in Madrid Saturday, with demonstrators demanding greater tenant protection. Widespread anger at rising housing costs have put pressure on Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez's government, which is expected to approve pro-tenant measures in its next cabinet meeting.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>At least 16 people killed as Russia and Ukraine trade deadly air strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f155015b972fdb860e69107fe9855e7c2f7d1a7a111919fd5c51bb07e87318</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:40:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-at-least-16-people-killed-as-russia-and-ukraine-trade-deadly-air-strikes--55f3b33690aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-at-least-16-people-killed-as-russia-and-ukraine-trade-deadly-air-strikes" /><summary type="html">At least 16 people were killed over the past 24 hours as Russia and Ukraine traded deadly drone and missile strikes, authorities from both countries said Saturday. The UN has warned of rising civilian deaths as Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV prays for France at Lourdes pilgrimage site</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc6b9929ddc431cc82491d103c80feec39ce647b10762687148bf70ee7ad844b</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T06:59:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-live-more-than-half-a-million-expected-at-pope-s-open-air-mass-in-paris--4ded6b6b0a9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260926-live-more-than-half-a-million-expected-at-pope-s-open-air-mass-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Saturday prayed that France receive “the gift of fraternal harmony” at the Grotto of Massabielle in Lourdes, a renowned pilgrimage site where Catholic tradition holds that the Virgin Mary appeared in 1858 to a peasant girl. The pontiff earlier said an open-air Mass in central Paris that drew an estimated 800,000 people. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU releases €6.6 billion for members arming Ukraine as seven killed in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdc90518baefa80a81c006cd37af0c1276a32be24b901bb129a1577c46c45b82</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T17:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-_6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv--228cd20fb306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-%E2%82%AC6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">European Union countries have agreed to release €6.6 billion from a fund meant to reimburse member states that have  provided arms to Ukraine, EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said on Friday. At least seven people were killed in Russian strikes on Kyiv earlier in the day, according to local authorities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU vows to pursue €120 million fine on X after US backs Musk's court challenge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fe84ce40739efb3ff4ebf712c2eb33402b1533cbebb4d46e7a2b90e483437b1</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:01:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-_120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge--67ad47c60d3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-%E2%82%AC120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Friday said it will pursue a €120 million fine against the X social network after the US Justice Department said it supported the efforts of X owner Elon Musk to have the case annulled. The bloc fined the platform in 2025 for breaching EU online transparency rules, notably with its pay-to-play blue "verification" checkmark.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Moldova is the best performer in my class': EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a7071ca8d1e86a50c5ddf4ef8cc3382fbc05e0a8ee5414085401c3cb61ceb9a</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:54:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos--14965558a28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos" /><summary type="html">The EU has gone through seven waves of enlargement since 1973, but there has not been one since Croatia joined in 2013. Indeed, there are not likely to be any new members in the club before 2028 – some 15 years after Croatia entered. But 2026 undeniably has momentum, and is on track to be a record year in terms of opening and closing new chapters for existing applicants. That is why our guest, EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos, sees this as "the year of the enlargement."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Climate breakdown: Is the EU adapting to the new normal? Europe's summer of disasters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91bf682ffe2278db6c84222bec8385b7b4f0508b18a73510b80071d76a9e3783</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters--f8e97073c504.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters" /><summary type="html">It has been called Europe's disaster year. 2026 has seen more than 30,000 excess deaths linked to heatwaves, along with mega wildfires, nuclear power plants having to shut down, gas plants under pressure, droughts reducing hydropower generation from rivers and wild fluctuations in electricity prices, not to mention major disruptions to crops and farming in general.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump made ‘final decision’ to allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ae867cf1701c81572965bccf4547d18e06edffb5bd2a9cea6fe1f34a092c98</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:46:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says--92e787840dd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-trump-made-final-decision-to-give-ukraine-patriot-licence-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump told President Volodymyr Zelensky that he had made a "final decision" to grant Kyiv the licence to produce Patriot air defence missiles, the Ukrainian leader said Friday. The assurance came during the last meeting between the two leaders, Zelensky said, capping a period of uncertainty after a series of reversals on the issue.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>From 'Jungle' to jungles, migrants in Calais continue to dream of UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08f2d2aa16e4542e57c528f8005b86fdd230bf1e692cedaae25c8bf94452df9e</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:30:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk--93cc7b8e4722.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260925-from-jungle-to-jungles-migrants-in-calais-continue-to-dream-of-uk" /><summary type="html">October 2026 marks 10 years since the Calais "Jungle" in northern France was dismantled by French police. The camp was home to thousands of migrants who wanted to cross the Channel and reach the UK. A decade on, migrants continue to dream of reaching British shores and the "Jungle" has been replaced by many smaller jungles scattered along the northern French coastline. FRANCE 24's Pauline Godart, Claire Paccalin and Mohamed Farhat report.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV’s visit to France: What you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:298013035eaeca47c22febd8dc09d4aceef4018b7774eef3fd5801942fdec85e</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:50:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit-to-france-what-you-need-to-know--963416a8ae42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit-to-france-what-you-need-to-know" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Friday arrives in France for a four-day visit – his fifth Apostolic journey since becoming pontiff last year – during which he hopes to repair the Catholic Church’s standing after sexual abuse scandals while also addressing issues such as the need to regulate AI. FRANCE 24 guides you through his visit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Most powerful force is human potential': Ukraine's military prioritises new tactics, technologies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc165b04cb8167684705c93afb4f4e4ba5907de645808bf5d3d95b29b6aefaec</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260925-our-most-powerful-force-is-human-potential-ukraine-military-prioritises-new-tactics-technol--bb5590fdf2b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260925-our-most-powerful-force-is-human-potential-ukraine-military-prioritises-new-tactics-technologies" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Kyrylo Berkal, Deputy Commander of Ukraine's Third Army Corps. He sees Ukraine’s struggle centred on human potential, adaptation and will. While Ukraine is outnumbered, outgunned and sometimes outflanked, their answer is to make human initiative a weapon: giving soldiers and sergeants room to innovate, developing technology from the tactical level upward, and trying to outthink their adversary. Berkal says that Operation Vivaldi embodies that philosophy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo finishes first day of France tour with youth vigil at Paris stadium</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2352e4e912b1c1df50b843b568910247baf8d48755b20aab2530024d01101028</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:57:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years--58e532ec129c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years" /><summary type="html">An estimated 80,000 people welcomed Pope Leo XIV to the Stade de France stadium in Saint-Denis near Paris on Friday. The pontiff warned earlier in the day that an AI "paradise of machines" risked undermining humanity in a speech at the Élysée presidential palace. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Schism with rebel Catholic sect casts a pall over Pope Leo’s visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c04669a105032e293756e014f6bad2e63490f6d31662ce7610f079bdbcab961</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes--83fe705c42fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes" /><summary type="html">The Vatican’s recent excommunication of followers of a Catholic splinter sect, the Society of Saint Pius X, has revived a longstanding feud within the Roman Catholic Church ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s state visit to France. The ultra-conservative group has established an extensive network of schools and has attracted thousands of followers in France.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU sanctions Russian pundit Xenia Fedorova after expulsion from France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2f0c434039a036f66c6904112f5013f4bf5f918953202a4c3dd9a6cac3eda21</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:45:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france--257744e3539a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Thursday imposed sanctions on Russian commentator Xenia Fedorova, whom France expelled in August over claims that she was disseminating "pro-Russian narratives" in the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>‘Massive, maximum destruction’: Putin seeks to bring Ukrainian civilians ‘to their knees’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60ce5973b3f5e7202933176427d8794d3883bf473c0e34e25bcc4d602f80ff47</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:17:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees--80c7cbe71ca4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/massive-maximum-destruction-putin-seeks-to-bring-ukrainian-civilians-to-their-knees" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev from Kyiv, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative. According to Zalmayev, Russia’s ongoing attacks on Ukraine reflect a broader political logic in which military force, political objectives and territorial ambitions are intertwined as instruments of Russian strategy. He argues that Moscow’s attacks on civilian infrastructure are designed to exert extreme pressure on Ukrainian society while demonstrating fierce retaliation to domestic audiences in Russia. Zalmayev contrasts this with Ukraine’s strikes on Russian energy infrastructure, which he describes as targeting assets that directly sustain Moscow’s war effort.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia slams Kyiv with ballistic missiles as Ukrainians brace for harsh winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88ddee564c032afed7aa67d77687f0ff550a6ec5d339100d780a6cca2f138723</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T05:31:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-as-moscow-steps-up-attacks-kyiv-residents-brace-for-harsh-winter--19e70fb342f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-as-moscow-steps-up-attacks-kyiv-residents-brace-for-harsh-winter" /><summary type="html">Russia on Thursday hit Kyiv with ballistic missiles and drones, killing two people, while a strike on a farm in the Kharkiv region killed six, according to Ukrainian officials. As autumn approaches, Ukrainians are bracing for a tough winter following Moscow's intensifying attacks on the country's energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Ukrainian President Zelensky addresses the UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edf0cca0e599224a2bfef5de93ab4a34d6fd4a49c293ff0e8501dd67076ba64b</id><updated>2026-09-28T16:50:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly--ac3edf47a818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urged the world’s leaders Wednesday to keep choking Russia’s revenues and impede its war efforts, telling the UN General Assembly that “Russia’s revenues must remain a target”. Watch his full speech above.</summary></entry></feed>
